Proposed redesign :

The redesigned playlist system uses two collections:
1. ArrayList: Stores the main playlist and supports accessing songs using indexes.
2. ArrayDeque: Manages the Up Next queue, allowing songs to be added at either end and removed from the front.

Performance comparison : 
Operation	                Original ArrayList	        Redesigned ArrayDeque
Add at end	                O(1) amortized	            O(1) amortized
Add at beginning	        O(n)	                    O(1) amortized
Remove at beginning	        O(n)	                    O(1) amortized
Access by index	            O(1)	                    Not supported
Iteration	                O(n)	                    O(n)

Analysis and discussion :

The original implementation uses ArrayList for all playlist operations. When a new song is inserted or removed from the beginning, the remaining elements must be shifted. This increases the execution time as the playlist grows.
The redesigned implementation uses ArrayDeque for front and rear operations. It avoids shifting all existing elements and provides efficient queue operations.

